# Inkling-2-Mini on ONE gfx1030 card (V620, 29.98 GiB), TP=1, with DSpark speculative decoding: the
# model's own draft (mtp.safetensors, which has to sit in the checkpoint directory) proposes 7
# tokens per step and the engine verifies 2 of them. Everything else is inkling2-mini-tp1:
# FULL_AND_PIECEWISE HIP graphs, prefix caching, one image per prompt. Draft, kernels, measured
# tables and the equality with the no-draft output: docs/rdna2/inkling2-dspark.md.
#
#   bash tools/rdna/serve_rdna.sh RECIPE=inkling2-mini-tp1-dspark MODEL=/path/to/inkling2-mini \
#     VENV=/path/to/venv HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=3
#
# Override any key after RECIPE= or in the caller's environment (both win over this file and over
# inkling2-mini-tp1), e.g. SEQS=8 SPEC_CONFIG='...[[1,2,2],[3,8,0]]...' keeps the draft for one or
# two requests and drops it from three, or MAXLEN=120000.
#
# Decode ms per token of one request on this engine, no draft -> K = 2 (3 prompts of each kind of
# text, 160 tokens, greedy): chat 17.5 -> 15.4 (1.14x), prose 1.09x, code 1.23x, structured 1.47x,
# edits of a file 1.51x, questions on a given document 1.59x; the mean of the six 17.7 -> 13.5
# (1.31x), and 1.27x on 33 held-out prompts. Two requests at once gain about 1.1x (chat 23.4 ->
# 21.3), three or more lose (0.95x),
# so SEQS is 2. The draft costs memory: 0.9 GiB of weights, 4 KiB of KV per token and 0.6 GiB of
# graphs, so the KV cache holds 125,597 tokens at SEQS 2 (185,568 without the draft); MAXLEN 125000
# fits with 0.5 % to spare: lower it if the engine refuses to start on a card with less free memory.
# The model requires num_speculative_tokens 7 (the draft block is 8 rows); the schedule [[1,2,2]]
# is the number of those 7 the engine verifies per step for 1..2 requests.

# shellcheck source=tools/rdna/recipes/inkling2-mini-tp1.env
source "$RDSE_RECIPES/inkling2-mini-tp1.env"

SEQS=2
MAXLEN=125000
SPEC_CONFIG='{"method":"dspark","num_speculative_tokens":7,"num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size":[[1,2,2]]}'
